# What a file another owner reads says joins the workspace (docs/extensions.md, "Owners and
# types"). csv-table, installed in the empty home by tests/drive.rs, answers file/read for
# Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv: each row as a one-row Markdown table, so the workspace's eruption type
# matches it and its [[links]] are links, and its Notes cell as Markdown, so its task is a task.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace
keys /
type krakatoa
wait-for Krakatoa
keys enter
# Krakatoa's backlinks list the CSV twice: the link in the task, and the one in the row.
wait-for ← Eruptions.csv  ☐ Read the Royal Society report on Krakatoa
expect ← Eruptions.csv  | Krakatoa | 1883 | 6 |
expect ←5 in
# Enter on one opens the table at the row the link is in.
click 24 80
wait-for backlinks · ↑↓ choose
click 24 80
wait-for Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv
keys e
wait-for Volcano: [[Krakatoa]]▏
keys esc esc
wait-for backlinks · ↑↓ choose
# The agenda lists the CSV's task with the notes' tasks, and opens the table at its row.
keys left A
wait-for ╭ Agenda
wait-for Read the Royal Society report on Krakatoa
expect Fri 20 Nov  Eruptions
screen
keys G k enter
wait-for Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv
keys e
wait-for Volcano: [[Krakatoa]]▏
keys esc esc esc
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
# Its rows are eruptions in the type's table, beside the rows of the table in a note.
keys i
wait-for eruption             8
type erup
wait-for rows · /erup
keys enter
wait-for 8 rows
expect Krakatoa
screen
keys esc
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
keys q
exits 0
